# sshd drop-in for huta's push transport (example; adapt the address range).
# One system user per dev box: huta-<box>, member of the group huta-push, no password, no sudo,
# no docker group. Every login runs huta-ssh, which hands one request to huta-push.socket; the
# host learns the box from the user's uid.
#
# Boxes are added and removed with huta, not here:
#   sudo huta enroll <box> --from <box ip> --pubkey '<key line>'   # user, pinned key, registry login
#   sudo huta revoke <box>
# `huta enroll` writes /var/lib/huta-ssh/<box>/.ssh/authorized_keys (root-owned, 0644) as
#   restrict,from="<box ip>" ssh-ed25519 AAAA… huta-push@<box>
# so each key works only from its box's address. This file never needs a per-box change.
#
# Allow every push user, but only from the tailnet (or whatever private range the boxes use).
# WARNING: as soon as any AllowUsers line exists, sshd lets in ONLY the users it lists. So put
# the pattern on the host's existing AllowUsers line, next to the admin users, and never add
# an AllowUsers line that lists only huta-* (that would lock out everyone else):
#   AllowUsers <existing users> huta-*@100.64.0.0/10
# The line is commented out here for that reason.
#AllowUsers <existing users> huta-*@100.64.0.0/10

Match User huta-*
    ForceCommand /usr/local/sbin/huta-ssh
    PermitTTY no
    AllowTcpForwarding no
    AllowAgentForwarding no
    AllowStreamLocalForwarding no
    X11Forwarding no
    PermitTunnel no
    PermitUserRC no
    LogLevel VERBOSE

# End the block explicitly: some sshd versions would apply it to everything after the include.
Match all
